  "lineage": "Music of the Fulɓe (Peul, Fulani) herding and fishing communities spread from the Senegal River valley through Mali, Niger and northern Cameroon, transmitted by gawlo praise singers and pastoral flute players and brought to record by Baaba Maal and Mansour Seck from the 1980s — slow to moderate free or loosely metered song built on the hoddu lute's short pentatonic cycles, bowed nyanyeru fiddle, overblown serdu flute doubled by the player's own hummed drone, and clear high melismatic solo singing in Pulaar over struck calabash.",
